            <ArticleTitle>Primary care and pain medicine. A community solution to the public health problem of chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>555-83, v</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author emphasizes that pain is an important public health problem that demands attention. He discusses ineffective management and its causes, administrative and socioeconomic problems perpetuating poor care, problems in technology transfer, organizational models, specialists and subspecialists, and other topics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
